  "notes": "OSM way spans Stockton->Powell and Geary->O'Farrell. Engine baseY = -8.26 (lowest corner at O'Farrell) while the Geary sidewalk is at -3.3..-5.0, so every Geary height is written relative to baseY: bow sidewalk burial 4.4 m -> storefront tops at 9.3 (=4.9 m visible), ground band 10.9 (=6.5 m), 1998 parapet 38.4 (=34 m), marble box top 46.2 (=43 m above its corner sidewalk), roof levels to 49.4 (=45 m). Geary edge 7 upper wall is 'none' and is clad by masses: 6 m + 8 m granite piers, 19 m (5-bay) and 13 m (3-bay) aluminium/glass wings, faceted 13 m bow projecting 2 m (glass_tint), 233 Geary white-marble box with a 7x7 punched grid, and the set-back 1929 roof levels. Missing engine features (listed in report): rooftop 'macy's' logotype on the bow parapet (a fascia 'macys' sign sits over the entrance doors instead), 12 m entrance canopy (canopy_metal is pinned at baseY+3.4 which is below the sidewalk here), three roof flagpoles, Cheesecake Factory/Burger Bar plaques should sit at 3rd/4th floor on the piers (placed at fascia height on the pier bays). Dyson/Swarovski were mapped to the 285 Geary corner building; the 1998 building's east-wing carved-out bays were still 'for lease' Dec 2024 per photo 02.",
